title: A run is measured through its process group in /proc, and a running server's memory is read there too, without connecting to it.
pid: 8778c497-6b5c-49d9-bba2-fa8bc7ced8b1
body: |2-
  Learned 2026-11-15, measuring what this machine uses, to answer Jeff's
  question of the least machine to rent: [[id:71fea003-732f-4c14-ac71-b98bc05de105][the answer]].
  'tools/introspect/machine-measures/measure_run.py' (built then, not
  yet committed) runs one command in a session of its own, samples
  every half second the summed memory of every process in that session
  and the machine's MemAvailable, takes the CPU time from the reaped
  children's rusage, and kills the run if MemAvailable falls under 1 GiB.
  Its docstring says what it misses. Measure one thing at a time: Jeff
  works on this machine, and two runs would each slow the other.
contains:
- 6c080d84-5c18-413d-b235-67bab468bc79
- 022b6d8a-6c6a-4e19-a5e3-bdf038ae20bb
- 5fae791c-b9e8-4e83-ab93-941654e33ed3
- 0baad5db-57fc-47c5-8fa7-676354c1f5ab
